Experimental E2K (Elbrus) back end written by Claude
=====================================================

Everything under gcc/config/e2k/ and gcc/common/config/e2k/, the e2k
hunks in gcc/config.gcc, gcc/configure.ac, gcc/configure and
libgcc/config.host, and the changes to libgcc/config/e2k/ after its
import from MCST's GPL sources, on the branch "claudes-e2k-compiler",
were written by Claude (Anthropic's AI
model) as an experiment requested by the relcc2 project owner: build a
GCC back end from the relcc2 specification (spec/isa, spec/abi,
doc/gcc-port-plan.md) to find out what the specification is missing and
what had to be guessed.

It is NOT intended for contribution to GCC: GCC does not accept
AI-generated code.  The owner writes the real port by hand.

libgcc/config/e2k/ was imported verbatim from MCST's published GPL
runtime sources (lcc 1.29.16, internal-lcc-libs-open-source) in its own
commit, so MCST's code and Claude's changes can be told apart.  The
e2k hunks in libgcc/unwind.inc are MCST's (from the same sources),
ported to mainline by Claude.

State, design, build and test instructions: STATUS.claude.md.
